hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"215","On looking when proposing marriage: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to propose to a woman, so he sent a woman to her and said: Smell her sides of the mouth and look at her ankles."
"216","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Shabib ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, that [the Prophet] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he married off his daughters, would order that their husbands not approach them until they had bathed, and would order their husbands to do so."
"217","al-Hasan ibn Amr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Ziyad, meaning Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, he sought his wives' permission to be nursed in the house of Aishah, and they permitted him."
"218","Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hawari narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on one of his campaigns, saw a slave girl large of breast and belly, and said: What is this? They said: So-and-so bought her from the captives. He said: Does he have intercourse with her? They said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can he bequeath to it when he has betrayed it in its hearing and sight, or how can it bequeath to him when it is not of him? I have intended to curse him with a curse that will enter the grave with him. [He said:] And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed her child. Abu Dawud said: Its beginning is narrated with a connected chain, and this adds: And he freed her child."
"219","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Sumay' narrated to us. I heard Abu Razin al-Asadi saying: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: What do you think of the statement of Allah the Exalted: (Divorce is twice; then keeping with kindness or releasing with kindness)? He said: Then where is the third? He said: Releasing with kindness, [the third]."
"220","Ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a bedouin to marry a Muhajir woman. And al-Hasan used to say: If he stays with her in the town, there is no harm."
"221","Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to a youth from the kings of Yemen for his sister, and he married her to him, so he went to fetch her. When he came to his father, he said: You have married a woman of royal daughters to a commoner; he kept at him until he consented. So he brought her, and when he went in to her, she said: I seek refuge with Allah from you. So he said: You have indeed sought refuge with a Refuge, and he let her go."
"222","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, that Umm Habibah was succeeded in marriage by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Uthman ibn Affan married her to him in the land of Abyssinia, and her mother was the daughter of Abu al-As, the paternal aunt of Uthman ibn Affan."
